Third-party components
----------------------

None. Semaphore has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the group export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

The transport gap
-----------------

A LAN transport does exist in this estate — `lan-kit`, zero dependencies, SSE and POST — but it is not wired into this app. What ships here is a same-device bus, so the room logic runs and can be tested. The engine takes two copies of a
group and syncs them, which is the operation a hotspot link would carry, and the page runs both copies so the
catch-up can be seen and tested.

Not encrypted
-------------

Messages are plain text on each device. Nothing here is end-to-end encrypted, and the app does not claim it
is. If the group needs that, this is not the app for it yet.

Why the sequence is assigned at merge
-------------------------------------

Two devices both numbering their first message #1 loses one of them on the first sync. A message therefore
carries a unique id, and the sequence number is assigned when devices merge, ordered by time then id. That
bug was found by a test that synced two devices that had each posted once.
